                <h3>The Solution</h3>
                <p>A full audit mapped every page, form, payment path, and outside platform. The broken booking flow was fixed first, then the site was rebuilt in custom code with automated deployment and every money path tested before launch. Moving to custom code, instead of another builder, means every page, integration, and back-end update can be changed directly, with no platform limits on SEO, performance, or features.</p>

                <h4 class="subsection-title">Implementation Components</h4>
                <div class="implementation-grid">
                  <div class="implementation-item">
                    <strong>1. Revenue Paths Fixed First</strong>
                    <p>Broken payment links were replaced with integrated scheduling and payment, so clients book and pay in one step. Every offer got a clear page with a working checkout.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="implementation-item">
                    <strong>2. Asset and Content Recovery</strong>
                    <p>All 25 original images were recovered from the old site at full size and optimized from 8 MB to 1.6 MB. The full newsletter archive was exported, inventoried, and sorted into site content and book material.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="implementation-item">
                    <strong>3. Podcast Automation</strong>
                    <p>One podcast page pulls every episode from the show's feed, with search and filters. A scheduled twice-daily rebuild publishes new episodes with no manual work.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="implementation-item">
                    <strong>4. Owned Email Capture</strong>
                    <p>A custom sign-up pop-up with a 10% welcome offer sends subscribers through a secure serverless function to the email platform, which triggers an automated welcome email. No third-party branding or tracking scripts load on the site.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="implementation-item">
                    <strong>5. SEO-Safe Domain Migration</strong>
                    <p>Every legacy URL and the old sitemap were redirected one to one. DNS was switched without touching the business email records, and HTTPS was verified on launch.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="implementation-item">
                    <strong>6. Search, Analytics, and Accessibility</strong>
                    <p>Structured data for the person, events, courses, videos, podcast, and articles; consent-based GA4 with sign-up and lead events; a three-option cookie banner; and a WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility commitment, including reduced-motion support.</p>
