                <h3>The Challenge (Detailed)</h3>
                <ul>
                  <li>Only 3 pages indexed in Google, with redirect inconsistencies blocking the rest</li>
                  <li>A single long services page instead of focused, searchable pages per service and audience</li>
                  <li>Mobile PageSpeed score of 71, with a 5.6-second Largest Contentful Paint</li>
                  <li>Title tags too long, missing AI-readable site summary (llms.txt), and pages with too few internal links</li>
                  <li>An orphaned subdomain from an old landing page producing 404 errors in analytics</li>
                  <li>Blog posts stored as Markdown files in the codebase, so publishing meant editing code</li>
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div class="case-section">
                <h3>The Solution</h3>
                <p>We fixed the technical foundation first, restructured the site so each service and audience had its own focused page, made the site readable by AI tools, and moved the blog into a headless CMS while keeping the custom-coded front end.</p>

                <h4 class="subsection-title">Implementation Components</h4>
                <div class="implementation-grid">
                  <div class="implementation-item">
                    <strong>1. Indexing and Technical SEO</strong>
                    <p>Enforced consistent URLs site-wide to clear redirect issues in Search Console, cleaned up the sitemap, trimmed title tags, and removed the orphaned subdomain causing 404s.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="implementation-item">
                    <strong>2. Search-Ready Site Architecture</strong>
                    <p>Split one long services page into dedicated service pages plus audience landing pages for nonprofits and government contractors, each targeting realistic, niche search terms.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="implementation-item">
                    <strong>3. AEO and GEO</strong>
                    <p>Added an llms.txt file written to the llmstxt.org spec so AI tools can understand the site, and structured content around the questions buyers actually ask.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="implementation-item">
                    <strong>4. Performance</strong>
                    <p>Removed costly mobile effects that slowed the first paint while keeping the desktop design intact.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="implementation-item">
                    <strong>5. Blog Migration to Sanity CMS</strong>
                    <p>A custom migration script converted 9 Markdown posts into structured content and uploaded their images into Sanity. Posts are now written and published in a visual editor, while the site stays custom-coded and fast.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div class="implementation-item">
                    <strong>6. Accessibility and Analytics</strong>
                    <p>Resolved 12 critical issues from an accessibility audit and added GA4 event tracking for key conversions, such as audit-tool scans and leads.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

